<Layout
  title="Couples · Marry Mae · Erotic education for couples in Lisbon"
  description="In-person erotic education for couples in Lisbon or at your place. Start with a 4-hour taster or walk journey one in 10 hours. Every kind of couple welcome."
  ground="ink"
  current="couples"
  legalReview
>
  <!-- 1 · Hero -->
  <PageHero
    slot="hero"
    label="couples · in person · lisbon or at your place"
    headline="Come <em>together.</em>"
    intro="Erotic education for couples who want more than the version of sex they've been running on. In person, in the body and a lot hotter than you'd expect from anything with the word education in it."
    photo={{ caption: 'photo: a couple, foreheads touching · duotone', alt: 'A couple with their foreheads touching in black and blood red', tone: 'blood' }}
  >
    <div class="btn-pair" data-reveal>
      <a class="btn btn--solid" href={url('start')} data-magnetic>Start with the intake form →</a>
      <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#packages" data-magnetic>See the packages ↓</a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <!-- 2 · Where you are -->
  <section class="on-paper section--quiet" aria-labelledby="where-title">
    <div class="container split split--sticky">
      <h2 id="where-title" class="display-m" data-split>Let me guess <em>where you are.</em></h2>
      <div class="prose" data-stagger>
        <p>Let me guess.</p>
        <p>You love each other. You still want each other (most days). And somewhere along the way, sex got a little bit beige.</p>
        <p>Maybe it's routine. Maybe it's rushed. Maybe one of you wants more and doesn't quite know how to say it. Maybe there's a baby, an affair, a new agreement or just years of life sitting on the bed between you.</p>
        <p>Or maybe you're brand new, still in the delicious bit and you already know you want support to keep it that way or deepen it from the start.</p>
        <p>Here's the thing: heart and sex rarely end up in the same bed. It takes a little know-how. And know-how can be learned.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Who comes to me -->
  <section class="on-flesh section--quiet" aria-labelledby="who-title">
    <div class="container split">
      <h2 id="who-title" class="display-m" data-split>Every kind of couple. <em>Every kind of hungry.</em></h2>
      <div class="prose" data-stagger>
        <p>Long-term couples who want the heat back. New couples who want to start the way they mean to go on. Queer couples. Non-monogamous couples and couples opening up. Couples after a baby, after an affair, after a long dry spell. Couples who've done the workshops, the temples, the play parties and are ready to go further.</p>
        <p>What you have in common: you want a life in the erotic world. More range, more depth, more of what's possible in the bedroom and well beyond it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Beginners and deep-enders -->
  <section class="on-paper section--quiet" aria-labelledby="feral-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="feral-title" class="display-m columns-title" data-split>Brand new to this or <em>already a little expertised?</em></h2>
      <div class="columns" data-stagger>
        <div class="column">
          <p><strong>If this is all new:</strong> you don't need to know anything and you don't need to be good at anything. We start slow (slower than you think) and you'll be surprised how much is already there between you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
          <p><strong>If you've done the work:</strong> you know your way around a breath practice and a consent conversation. Good. We move through the groundwork faster and spend our hours where it gets interesting. Energy, range, edge, the parts most workshops never reach.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="columns-foot body-l" data-reveal>Either way, you walk the same six steps. How fast and how deep is up to you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · What happens in the room -->
  <section class="on-ink section--quiet" aria-labelledby="room-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <h2 id="room-title" class="display-m" data-split>What happens in the room. <em>(Mostly.)</em></h2>
        <div class="prose" data-stagger>
          <p>Every session has the same shape. We open, we move, we close.</p>
          <p>We open by arriving. You leave the outside world at the door, drop into your bodies and we make our agreements about what's part of today.</p>
          <p>We move through the six steps: Slow, Feel, Speak, Meet, Flow, Tend. You slow down together, notice what's actually there, name the things that never got said and get seen by each other. And then the erotic current usually takes it from there. What exactly that looks like? Every imprint is unique and so is every erotic unfolding. (Some things are better felt than read.)</p>
          <p>We close properly and you go home with something to practise that came out of your own session.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="touch-box" data-reveal>
        <span class="label">about touch, plainly</span>
        <ul>
          <li>You touch each other. That's the centre of the work.</li>
          <li>I teach, guide and demonstrate and I work hands-on with you too, for example giving a massage together with one of you while the other learns.</li>
          <li>You don't touch me. In the deep end that’s different.</li>
          <li>Everything is agreed before we start, in writing. Either of you can say yes, no or wait at any moment. Strong agreements are in place, always.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="touch-foot body-l" data-reveal>This is erotic education: you come to learn, practise and take it home.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · The packages -->
